 this explicit either-agree-or-exit behavior. Do not quietly re-enable a
 dismissible banner as an SEO optimization.
 
+The wall has no dead end and no gap in front of it (deep audit 2026-11-09,
+findings A3 and A4):
+
+- **Go back is a transition, not an end state.** Both answers are set aside
+  only while the browser leaves. A document the browser keeps and shows again
+  (the back/forward cache: Go back, then Forward), a step back that stays in
+  the same document, or a history with nothing behind the entry asks again
+  with both answers working; after a Go back that went nowhere, the next one
+  leaves by the referrer or a blank page.
+- **Only a recorded agreement takes a standing wall down.** Agreement given on
+  the Privacy Policy page, in another tab, on another McCluster host, or held
+  in the arriving member's own account record is read when the page is shown,
+  focused or told of the change, and the wall comes down where it stands,
+  once. Go back, Escape, a timeout and a failed sign-in handoff never do.
+  As with agreeing on the Privacy Policy page, analytics start with the next
+  page.
+- **A sign-in being carried in waits behind the wall.** A page opened with
+  `#mcc_handoff=` is concealed at once and shows one status line with no
+  answers. It ends in entry on the member's own record, or in the question:
+  ten seconds without word of the sign-in is the limit, and four more for a
+  page that reloads signed in.
+
+Unit and contract coverage is in `scripts/test/account-identity-gate.test.mjs`
+and `scripts/test/privacy-notice-policy.test.mjs`; the real-browser journeys,
+including a real back/forward-cache restore in full Chromium, are in
+`scripts/e2e/music-world-continuity.e2e.mjs`. WebKit and iPad Safari are not
+covered by any automated run.
